**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Relation** |
|----------|----------|-------------|----------------|--------------|
| **G1 – Deliver Resources** | The overall mission: collect the requested resources from storage and deliver them to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` (sequential) | Perform | AND |
| **G2 – Collection Phase** | Robot gathers the required resources from one or more storages following the order defined by waiting‑time + path estimation. | `;` | Perform | AND |
| **G2.1 – Navigate to Storage** | Robot moves from its current location to the designated storage. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G2.2 – Request Resource** | Robot sends a message to the storage specifying the exact resources needed. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G2.3 – Wait for Retrieval** | Robot waits until the storage has retrieved the requested resources. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G2.4 – Monitor Battery (Collection)** | Robot continuously monitors its battery level while in the collection phase. | `-` | Query | AND |
| **G2.5 – Handle Low Battery** | If battery < 10 % robot returns to the recharge station, recharges, and assigns the remaining mission to another robot. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G3 – Delivery Phase** | Robot transports the retrieved resources from storage to the specified delivery location. | `;` | Perform | AND |
| **G3.1 – Navigate to Destination** | Robot moves from its current location to the delivery location. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G3.2 – Deliver Resource** | Robot transfers the resources to the requesting agent at the destination. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G3.3 – Return to Checkpoint** | If battery < 30 % during delivery, robot returns the resource to the nearest checkpoint. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G3.4 – Assign Remaining Task** | Robot informs another robot about the remaining resources and their positions so that it can continue the delivery. | `-` | Perform | AND |
| **G3.5 – Monitor Battery (Delivery)** | Robot continuously monitors its battery level while in the delivery phase. | `-` | Query | AND |
| **G3.6 – Handle Failure to Return Resource** | If the robot fails to return the resource to a checkpoint, it triggers an alert and sends a report to the sector manager. | `-` | Perform | AND |

---

### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|------------------------|
| **AT1 – Navigate to Storage** | Move from current location to the nearest storage. | AND | `Storage` | 1 |
| **AT2 – Request Resource** | Send request message with resource specification to the storage. | AND | `Storage` | 1 |
| **AT3 – Wait for Retrieval** | Await until the storage has retrieved the resources. | AND | `Storage` | 1 |
| **AT4 – Monitor Battery (Collection)** | Continuously read battery level during collection. | AND | `Collection Phase` | 1 |
| **AT5 – Recharge & Reassign** | Return to recharge station, charge, then assign the remaining mission to another robot. | AND | `Recharge Station` | 1 |
| **AT6 – Navigate to Destination** | Move from current location to the delivery destination. | AND | `Destination` | 1 |
| **AT7 – Deliver Resource** | Transfer resources to the requesting agent at the destination. | AND | `Destination` | 1 |
| **AT8 – Return to Checkpoint** | Return the resource to the nearest checkpoint (if battery < 30 %). | AND | `Checkpoint` | 1 |
| **AT9 – Inform Next Robot** | Communicate remaining resources and positions to another robot. | AND | `Checkpoint` | 1 |
| **AT10 – Monitor Battery (Delivery)** | Continuously read battery level during delivery. | AND | `Delivery Phase` | 1 |
| **AT11 – Alert & Report** | Trigger alert and send failure report to sector manager. | AND | `Sector Manager` | 1 |

